ail":"callum.hall@gamma.co.uk","name":"Callum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:32:53Z","email":"callum.hall@gamma.co.uk","name":"Callum"},"message":"feat(chat-widget): widget shell + Ask library tab (#159)\n\nAdds ChatWidgetProvider (open/closed, active tab, draft, lastBookId)\nmounted alongside UsageProvider, and a launcher + panel visible on\nevery screen. The Ask library tab relocates today''s one-shot Q&A\n(streaming answer, citations, retrieved passages, limit handling)\ninto the widget, functionally identical to QueryScreen. The old /ask\nroute, QueryScreen, and ask-again.ts are untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016VgTix8cdJ1CwZQhpFpiPc","tree":{"sha":"74493a57cd0f0aa2ebda7485646ace43cd903c51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cal3574/scriptorium/git/trees/74493a57cd0f0aa2ebda7485646ace43cd903c51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cal3574/scriptorium/git/commits/e812662911538dbc81826ee57ca511fe3367cd96","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286878949?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/calhallgamma","id":286878949,"login":"calhallgamma","node_id":"U_kgDOERls5Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Cal3574/scriptorium/commit/e812662911538dbc81826ee57ca511fe3367cd96","node_id":"C_kwDOUIpLSdoAKGU4MTI2NjI5MTE1MzhkYmM4MTgyNmVlNTdjYTUxMWZlMzM2N2NkOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Cal3574/scriptorium/commit/063226ba6d722df0109eeade54daa5af7be71953","sha":"063226ba6d722df0109eeade54daa5af7be71953","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cal3574/scriptorium/commits/063226ba6d722df0109eeade54daa5af7be71953"}],"sha":"e812662911538dbc81826ee57ca511fe3367cd96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cal3574/scriptorium/commits/e812662911538dbc81826ee57ca511fe3367cd96"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286878949?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/calhallgamma","id":286878949,"login":"calhallgamma","node_id":"U_kgDOERls5Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/calhallgamma","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cal3574/scriptorium/commits/34a9a5b8bc1aadb0ed3cfb4715417b729016acb5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:07:18Z","email":"callum.hall@gamma.co.uk","name":"Callum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:09:20Z","email":"callum.hall@gamma.co.uk","name":"Callum"},"message":"feat(agent): context-window trimming for long-running threads\n\nAdds hybrid trimming to the reading-companion Agent conversation so a thread\nthat grows very long stays coherent and cheap to run, without ever delaying\nthe visible reply.\n\n- Triggered by a message-count `COUNT` (40 rows since the last summarization\n  boundary), matching the repo''s existing usage-tracking pattern - no\n  token-counting utility needed.\n- Hybrid: the most recent 10 completed turns are kept and replayed verbatim;\n  everything older is folded into a single rolling summary on the thread\n  record, regenerated (not appended) each time the threshold re-crosses.\n- The thread''s opening highlight-to-discuss turn is always additionally\n  pinned into the prompt verbatim, regardless of age.\n- Runs synchronously in `AgentService.run`, but only after `agent_done` has\n  already been yielded - by the time the SSE pump resumes the generator to\n  find out it''s done, the reply is already on the wire, so trimming never\n  delays it.\n- The boundary is tracked by `agent_messages.seq`, not a timestamp - the same\n  same-tick-tie problem `seq` was already added to solve for turn adjacency.\n- `agent_threads` gains nullable `running_summary` / `summarized_through_seq`\n  columns, both untouched until a thread first crosses the threshold.\n- `FakeLlmClient` gains a summarization-shape branch so the trim''s LLM call\n  runs end to end offline.\n\nCloses #158\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016VgTix8cdJ1CwZQhpFpiPc","tree":{"sha":"5c625d109481283ebbbe9b3a6ec4bc24ac786a31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cal3574/scriptorium/git/trees/5c625d109481283ebbbe9b3a6ec4bc24ac786a31"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cal3574/scriptorium/git/commits/34a9a5b8bc1aadb0ed3cfb4715417b729016acb5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"ve