ists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commit/1080df2e1a61db145b76022591e076aa14dbdbaa","node_id":"C_kwDOUJVo4NoAKDEwODBkZjJlMWE2MWRiMTQ1Yjc2MDIyNTkxZTA3NmFhMTRkYmRiYWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commit/5b767911733c3571e49b7b756feca5341f3f069a","sha":"5b767911733c3571e49b7b756feca5341f3f069a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/5b767911733c3571e49b7b756feca5341f3f069a"}],"sha":"1080df2e1a61db145b76022591e076aa14dbdbaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/1080df2e1a61db145b76022591e076aa14dbdbaa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139071865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru","id":139071865,"login":"jessiicamaru","node_id":"U_kgDOCEoReQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/5b767911733c3571e49b7b756feca5341f3f069a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:28:49Z","email":"139071865+jessiicamaru@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dũng Hoàng"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:28:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deps): MassTransit back on 8.3.6 after a broker outage stopped consumers for good (#354)\n\nOn MassTransit 8.5.11 (#326) a RabbitMQ outage under load stopped receive endpoints for good - Inventory''s ReserveInventory, three of Order''s queues - leaving them with messages and 0 consumers and every new order Submitted until a restart: 3 of 3 runs, 0 of 7 on 8.3.6, and not specs/154''s reconnect policy. Every MassTransit* reference is back on 8.3.6 (the other updates of #326 stay), Dependabot ignores MassTransit minors as well as majors, and MassTransitVersionTests fails on any other version in any csproj or in what the build resolved, since CI cannot see the defect. fault.sh broker on the rebuilt stack: 5 of 5 passed, every order paid, error queues empty, no queue left without a consumer, every service reconnected within 4.4 s of the port opening. The cause in 8.5 stays open (a cancelled consume ending ReceiveTransportAgent.Run). Closes #353.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6e15ee6535ff161a24d40a7fbdfdb13f7733290f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/git/trees/6e15ee6535ff161a24d40a7fbdfdb13f7733290f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/git/commits/5b767911733c3571e49b7b756feca5341f3f069a","verification":{"payload":"tree 6e15ee6535ff161a24d40a7fbdfdb13f7733290f\nparent 9af65c8809e7853044e2182831e602aad3652b57\nauthor Dũng Hoàng <139071865+jessiicamaru@users.noreply.github.com> 1791289729 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791289729 +0700\n\nfix(deps): MassTransit back on 8.3.6 after a broker outage stopped consumers for good (#354)\n\nOn MassTransit 8.5.11 (#326) a RabbitMQ outage under load stopped receive endpoints for good - Inventory''s ReserveInventory, three of Order''s queues - leaving them with messages and 0 consumers and every new order Submitted until a restart: 3 of 3 runs, 0 of 7 on 8.3.6, and not specs/154''s reconnect policy. Every MassTransit* reference is back on 8.3.6 (the other updates of #326 stay), Dependabot ignores MassTransit minors as well as majors, and MassTransitVersionTests fails on any other version in any csproj or in what the build resolved, since CI cannot see the defect. fault.sh broker on the rebuilt stack: 5 of 5 passed, every order paid, error queues empty, no queue left without a consumer, every service reconnected within 4.4 s of the port opening. The cause in 8.5 stays open (a cancelled consume ending ReceiveTransportAgent.Run). Closes #353.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxOmCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALK4QABS3CTbFyYauSVAyt2rduBOA\n/fvO8CCnmBPDKgqpsJzADAHsErsh/jDr4pERXcRj2xWZe8v6y05yPTpBubDTyBbD\nSIjKyVhwDMFG8mTnzftd01N0Zp2BFEJCG8kmEl2SGI8J4Wv61XP10KomvWFXNKHL\nYCkf5u5mw9cfYWGMCXfSjDdW/+E/YKyt1DttBB7V0X7Ccdr0KQejKjNIrULsLp6c\nY0Ss+KDMAYM6+F4sLcMHfYEqTJ8RFYmYNzfrT+4EKOW48s9bE7XTItDPzvQt6BhQ\nFkzzHTMqoeQZGEmlNXsoCEG2V8TGkgah8VMlfgI8ZO/cgv08dWmljPAkW8oAgv8F\nRp5UEyIT7LuHS6SBrmATh333emsyOMLlyvXFmmZC1dsB3nZH/ASN4LYE/AnZDn7P\nDI9EflTYhC0mswbDohsidJs2/Oy67XHzpEg8wneqztos7UBdlvLl1b45yl9lY8hQ\nlcl+wX+DIyarxlNdT9vxZSwBZ4I44rdrZ56TeZNwa7qskcYwUou+5YRlJsRgumo/\nZyXbOmOrXGXa0MOXdIIdx46Ixq8Ra23/t+0kp/XYMYug72NinSF2BTB27MtMKR/f\njfG61wCjMUf8L3Ib6/gkBxcs9JEJycUNH0fONZGQcfHzp3eWBj5RdY/Q4ugWLZLk\n1q6oNK3Olutt/JHrqS7e\n=/xFR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T12:28:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commit/5b767911733c3571e49b7b756feca5341f3f069a","node_id":"C_kwDOUJVo4NoAKDViNzY3OTExNzMzYzM1NzFlNDliN2I3NTZmZWNhNTM0MWYzZjA2OWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commit/9af65c8809e7853044e2182831e602aad3652b57","sha":"9af65c8809e7853044e2182831e602aad3652b57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/9af65c8809e7853044e2182831e602aad3652b57"}],"sha":"5b767911733c3571e49b7b756feca5341f3f069a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/5b767911733c3571e49b7b756feca5341f3f069a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139071865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru","id":139071865,"login":"jessiicamaru","node_id":"U_kgDOCEoReQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/9af65c8809e7853044e2182831e602aad3652b57/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T04:53:15Z","email":"139071865+jessiicamaru@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dũng Hoàng"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T04:53:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(shared): services reconnect to the broker within seconds of its return (#352)\n\nMassTransit 8.3-8.5 retries a lost RabbitMQ connection up to 30 s apart (fixed in its host configuration) and the bus outbox waits for every endpoint; cfg.ReconnectQuickly puts the transport''s own filters on a 1-5 s schedule (Messaging__ReconnectQuickly=false restores the default; BrokerReconnectTests fails if MassTransit''s internals change). The broker''s health check is now check_port_connectivity - ping passed before RabbitMQ opened its port 27-80 s after start - and fault.sh measures from the port opening. A/B on one stack: every service back within 5.96, 4.33, 3.85 s of the port opening, against 28.79, 28.43, 30.70, 6.36 s with MassTransit''s schedule. Closes #304.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e4b6d2ef8b236472cdffee12be7e51b2dace8e63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/git/trees/e4b6d2ef8b236472cdffee12be7e51b2dace8e63"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/git/commits/9af65c8809e7853044e2182831e602aad3652b57","verification":{"payload":"tree e4b6d2ef8b236472cdffee12be7e51b2dace8e63\nparent 9beeffa094f93514fa48e43e53e518bcef3e1946\nauthor Dũng Hoàng <139071865+jessiicamaru@users.noreply.github.com> 1791262395 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791262395 +0700\n\nfix(shared): services reconnect to the broker within seconds of its return (#352)\n\nMassTransit 8.3-8.5 retries a lost RabbitMQ connection up to 30 s apart (fixed in its host configuration) and the bus outbox waits for every endpoint; cfg.ReconnectQuickly puts the transport''s own filters on a 1-5 s schedule (Messaging__ReconnectQuickly=false restores the default; BrokerReconnectTests fails if MassTransit''s internals change). The broker''s health check is now check_port_connectivity - ping passed before RabbitMQ opened its port 27-80 s after start - and fault.sh measures from the port opening. A/B on one stack: every service back within 5.96, 4.33, 3.85 s of the port opening, against 28.79, 28.43, 30.70, 6.36 s with MassTransit''s schedule. Closes #304.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxH67CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0SoQAFcky4W9iBqpJcOPbDDvnfyn\nCQ0ohCV6KM3imlH85fwlyMLYk2hWPdS5aGjZfqYleWy6yUS0zKcufD4IOOe7cwW4\nkrYRuY671Lj+I7rZu5RejKC5zJevQK/c3fL2CKC6kJ+0sSj8Blm7WH9Un/UBzNr5\nifh29ThVjX2CgZsFE3P02EjwWCFVnwNKsuz7KHFVhrnS3ZV0jNrne2V8yLvFzI38\n7P8DOGlPAZ0ug3R3nbXhz+oKYC66oiIW0GwhMegbh8M0/9YbTCYEvw/Frymk9xO3\nzzotbj47qm+UeH7EgeVgDQ4eMQjUE8JAKZ1jFIdVDNNWcN0uYsAG1GsJA7FchZBI\norz3zbThH6GQwh3pbSKHYOiIT6RjYRWgK+4r4Hu+Y7Yr3Xh72aR50