//api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru","id":139071865,"login":"jessiicamaru","node_id":"U_kgDOCEoReQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/1ebea7b1f41bdc6e4e680c78b72561ec64fb9192/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T13:38:14Z","email":"139071865+jessiicamaru@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dũng Hoàng"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T13:38:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: load-test checkout and measure it (#303)\n\nCloses #290. Three k6 scenarios against the compose stack, each one command (server/loadtest/run.sh race|checkout|browse), run from k6''s own container on the compose network: 100 customers racing for 20 units, 5 checkouts a second of one product for a minute, and anonymous browsing ramping to 50. Each prepares and cleans up its own data, checks its invariants through the API afterwards, and fails on a broken invariant or an unexpected response - never on latency. docs/testing/load-test-results.md is generated from the summaries kept in the repository. Final runs on main: the race sold exactly 20 of 20 three times; checkout paid every order with units deducted matching, three times; browse 109 requests a second with no errors; zero 40001 and every error queue empty. Their first runs found #299 and #301, both fixed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a802d3502e595d6f048d34736ec12d0717dd5670","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/git/trees/a802d3502e595d6f048d34736ec12d0717dd5670"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/git/commits/1ebea7b1f41bdc6e4e680c78b72561ec64fb9192","verification":{"payload":"tree a802d3502e595d6f048d34736ec12d0717dd5670\nparent d8ea56b841ee0346daed9337a8eb588355b70cbf\nauthor Dũng Hoàng <139071865+jessiicamaru@users.noreply.github.com> 1791034694 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791034694 +0700\n\ntest: load-test checkout and measure it (#303)\n\nCloses #290. Three k6 scenarios against the compose stack, each one command (server/loadtest/run.sh race|checkout|browse), run from k6''s own container on the compose network: 100 customers racing for 20 units, 5 checkouts a second of one product for a minute, and anonymous browsing ramping to 50. Each prepares and cleans up its own data, checks its invariants through the API afterwards, and fails on a broken invariant or an unexpected response - never on latency. docs/testing/load-test-results.md is generated from the summaries kept in the repository. Final runs on main: the race sold exactly 20 of 20 three times; checkout paid every order with units deducted matching, three times; browse 109 requests a second with no errors; zero 40001 and every error queue empty. Their first runs found #299 and #301, both fixed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwQVGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuj4QAIJ31W5higDjHD1Rnd8m5lRo\nIfHZU3T68yUTGIegndmTL/lbxJ6jPgTxk9h7vOnH+pYz36fg5cPYhOUQkVDSUx8N\nVn26DDfugGRkLFJhQ0dHtY58rrs018HM5eIBSGqNQfoMddtDbkrgWBUfRqHyiR7d\niJcVdHB4OrUI/c4+QFblqliCeYrGCG/zj5Xs/K9w+385yOR3uZiSmmLUrC7nkNj0\nHTE33DfuCObjn75utxu+KaJNaxsshcjjTwcK5ML6ywi+mlfPVxmRgd7p98sgwsnY\nLl5qB/nh