c78b72561ec64fb9192","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/1ebea7b1f41bdc6e4e680c78b72561ec64fb9192"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139071865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru","id":139071865,"login":"jessiicamaru","node_id":"U_kgDOCEoReQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/d8ea56b841ee0346daed9337a8eb588355b70cbf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T12:14:08Z","email":"139071865+jessiicamaru@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dũng Hoàng"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T12:14:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(inventory): consume at READ COMMITTED - no serialization aborts on a popular product (#302)\n\nCloses #301. Inventory''s EF outbox consumes at READ COMMITTED instead of MassTransit''s default REPEATABLE READ: a reservation locks the stock row FOR UPDATE, and REPEATABLE READ aborted every consume that waited for that lock (1,710-5,610 40001 per two-minute run on one popular product). READ COMMITTED is the isolation every Inventory handler already runs in, and is tested in, outside a consumer. Over eight warm runs: zero aborts, the same median, a tighter tail in 4 of 5 runs; every invariant held, every error queue empty. The remaining ceiling is the one stock row''s lock. The issue''s original 8.3 s premise was a cold start, corrected on the issue and in the records.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f6679dae423acb68cc1db98218a0ef69ea274ab5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/git/trees/f6679dae423acb68cc1db98218a0ef69ea274ab5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/git/commits/d8ea56b841ee0346daed9337a8eb588355b70cbf","verification":{"payload":"tree f6679dae423acb68cc1db98218a0ef69ea274ab5\nparent a769e2abe3cc6d998f13b4a1f942533365f6440e\nauthor Dũng Hoàng <139071865+jessiicamaru@users.noreply.github.com> 1791029648 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791029648 +0700\n\nfix(inventory): consume at READ COMMITTED - no serialization aborts on a popular product (#302)\n\nCloses #301. Inventory''s EF outbox consumes at READ COMMITTED instead of MassTransit''s default REPEATABLE READ: a reservation locks the stock row FOR UPDATE, and REPEATABLE READ aborted every consume that waited for that lock (1,710-5,610 40001 per two-minute run on one popular product). READ COMMITTED is the isolation every Inventory handler already runs in, and is tested in, outside a consumer. Over eight warm runs: zero aborts, the same median, a tighter tail in 4 of 5 runs; every invariant held, every error queue empty. The remaining ceiling is the one stock row''s lock. The issue''s original 8.3 s premise was a cold start, corrected on the issue and in the records.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwPGQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtdoQAJv/w3NjvkEKc1YKXssYgIYn\n7g6VFRil+GqDByDK0WvMsZBai1QTFF+7er5U+aqrMQ6zv3e4KCIkSL+fFcKY3oqi\nE