","html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru","id":139071865,"login":"jessiicamaru","node_id":"U_kgDOCEoReQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commit/0235eb98d3e48e324468dd1c29adb3bb9c8295ce","node_id":"C_kwDOUJVo4NoAKDAyMzVlYjk4ZDNlNDhlMzI0NDY4ZGQxYzI5YWRiM2JiOWM4Mjk1Y2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commit/0a3f72d91000394231612189031ab6ed221c179a","sha":"0a3f72d91000394231612189031ab6ed221c179a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/0a3f72d91000394231612189031ab6ed221c179a"}],"sha":"0235eb98d3e48e324468dd1c29adb3bb9c8295ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/0235eb98d3e48e324468dd1c29adb3bb9c8295ce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139071865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru","id":139071865,"login":"jessiicamaru","node_id":"U_kgDOCEoReQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/0a3f72d91000394231612189031ab6ed221c179a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:04:04Z","email":"139071865+jessiicamaru@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dũng Hoàng"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:04:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: staff sign in with a second factor (#230)\n\nCloses #218 - specs/110.\n\nStaff (Admin, Moderator) sign in with a code from an authenticator app (TOTP, RFC 6238); anybody else may. Staff\nroles are written into a token only for a session verified with a code, so every service refuses an unverified\nstaff session with no change outside Identity; staff without it are told SetupRequired.\n\nThe right password answers a hashed, five-minute, five-attempt challenge and nothing else; POST\n/api/auth/login/two-factor exchanges it with a code or one of ten hashed recovery codes. A code works once (a\nguarded TwoFactorLastStep); wrong codes count toward the email pause, which the password alone no longer clears.\nSecrets are sealed with AES-GCM under TWO_FACTOR_KEY, required at startup. An administrator resets another\nperson''s second factor - never their own - ending their sessions and emailing TwoFactorReset.\n\nStorefront: the second sign-in step, /account/two-factor with the QR code drawn in the browser, a banner for staff\nwho must set it up, and the reset on /admin/users. The verify scripts, the seed scripts, Bruno and Playwright\ncompute the administrator''s codes from ADMIN_TOTP_SECRET (development and CI only). Migration AddTwoFactor only\nadds. How TOTP works: docs/features/auth/totp-two-factor.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4eefdcca18ff80444c20e9e8dd4b687094f7f48c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/git/trees/4eefdcca18ff80444c20e9e8dd4b687094f7f48c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/git/commits/0a3f72d91000394231612189031ab6ed221c179a","verification":{"payload":"tree 4eefdcca18ff80444c20e9e8dd4b687094f7f48c\nparent fcd9e036c56d2747676a8c4fb4eb74c2cf22d7a2\nauthor Dũng Hoàng <139071865+jessiicamaru@users.noreply.github.com> 1790791444 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790791444 +0700\n\nfeat: staff sign in with a second factor (#230)\n\nCloses #218 - specs/110.\n\nStaff (Admin, Moderator) sign in with a code from an authenticator app (TOTP, RFC 6238); anybody else may. Staff\nroles are written into a token only for a session verified with a code, so every service refuses an unverified\nstaff session with no change outside Identity; staff without it are told SetupRequired.\n\nThe right password answers a hashed, five-minute, five-attempt challenge and nothing else; POST\n/api/auth/login/two-factor exchanges it with a code or one of ten hashed recovery codes. A code works once (a\nguarded TwoFactorLastStep); wrong codes count toward the email pause, which the password alone no longer clears.\nSecrets are sealed with AES-GCM under TWO_FACTOR_KEY, required at startup. An administrator resets another\nperson''s second factor - never their own - ending their sessions and emailing TwoFactorReset.\n\nStorefront: the second sign-in step, /account/two-factor with the QR code drawn in the browser, a banner for staff\nwho must set it up, and the reset on /admin/users. The verify scripts, the seed scripts, Bruno and Playwright\ncompute the administrator''s codes from ADMIN_TOTP_SECRET (development and CI only). Migration AddTwoFactor only\nadds. How TOTP works: docs/features/auth/totp-two-factor.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Cl