iicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/cffa020fefbc35d3ae1078b8035857621dcc51e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139071865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru","id":139071865,"login":"jessiicamaru","node_id":"U_kgDOCEoReQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/8a3503ce4e456db9351999ba6d023ff3e4f6095b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:20:27Z","email":"139071865+jessiicamaru@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dũng Hoàng"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:20:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: filter the catalogue by price and by what is in stock (#229)\n\nCloses #216 - specs/109.\n\nGET /api/products takes minPrice, maxPrice and inStock. A range is of the ''from'' price the card shows, in the\ncurrency asked for, never converted: products.Price over the partial IX_products_on_shelf_Price in the default\ncurrency; any other currency through the ids of a grouped join over that currency''s active variant prices\n(IX_variant_prices_Currency_Amount) - never a per-product subquery. inStock reads the availability read model. A\nreversed or negative range is 400. The catalogue has a price range and an In stock only switch, kept in the address.\nMigration AddCatalogueFilterIndexes adds two indexes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8528dfb3ad8ed2726abb3d2e348739cb006938c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/git/trees/8528dfb3ad8ed2726abb3d2e348739cb006938c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/git/commits/8a3503ce4e456db9351999ba6d023ff3e4f6095b","verification":{"payload":"tree 8528dfb3ad8ed2726abb3d2e348739cb006938c0\nparent 85e6bd0cb28d3a5c0e422b83eaa87765abd17641\nauthor Dũng Hoàng <139071865+jessiicamaru@users.noreply.github.com> 1790511627 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790511627 +0700\n\nfeat: filter the catalogue by price and by what is in stock (#229)\n\nCloses #216 - specs/109.\n\nGET /api/products takes minPrice, maxPrice and inStock. A range is of the ''from'' price the card shows, in the\ncurrency asked for, never converted: products.Price over the partial IX_products_on_shelf_Price in the default\ncurrency; any other currency through the ids of a grouped join over that currency''s active variant prices\n(IX_variant_prices_Currency_Amount) - never a per-product subquery. inStock reads the availability read model. A\nreversed or negative range is 400. The catalogue has a price range and an In stock only switch, kept in the address.\nMigration AddCatalogueFilterIndexes adds two indexes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquQoLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAADUQAIb//+1B7D2nqcfojVy0Ek+L\nAzDIVZiRRJhE/kPSsLs1bd4yMD2hQPoRHPjYFKIV2aNtGdoV2NbgeuOPsOj5S0VD\ni13l5wDQvqX7DyDw5+yugliyL3tzsc9pk8o531F0aoaMIQt7Iq12ngWMwRbKZRYz\ndO8FduEpvdnaAKwrAbMsno7XNiPvXRv6jpsvxFPSroO8JbyN9dL53eFqAgQ4h+oW\nPMJ7pNRE3KYQSGM2dqmixdE4NX4xb2hLW4DNUvjy9KV6PUZ0cJVMLbNf