5ca38919469a1c07b40bec4960a8fa147367d82a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/5ca38919469a1c07b40bec4960a8fa147367d82a"}],"sha":"6f42a94682686fda729fcd894a0bb708104d0310","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/6f42a94682686fda729fcd894a0bb708104d0310"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139071865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru","id":139071865,"login":"jessiicamaru","node_id":"U_kgDOCEoReQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/5ca38919469a1c07b40bec4960a8fa147367d82a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T00:27:14Z","email":"139071865+jessiicamaru@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dũng Hoàng"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T00:27:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(catalog): a banned seller''s shop is closed (#202)\n\nA banned seller''s products stayed on sale; their orders became sales nobody could ship (#193).\n\nIdentity publishes SellerSuspensionChangedEvent in the ban''s transaction for a seller, and\nagain when the ban is lifted; a lock closes nothing. Catalog records it on its sellers read\nmodel with an upsert guarded on the decision''s time and copies it onto the seller''s products\n(products.SellerSuspended), so Product.OnShelf answers no for the listing, lookup, images,\nreviews, questions, saving and both pricing paths. Reopening tells savers of products back on\nsale. Approving a banned applicant''s shop is 409; the users page reads \"Banned · shop closed\".\nMigration SellerSuspension is expand-only.\n\nDecided on the user''s behalf: a ban closes the shop and a lock does not; the suspension is a\nread model that decides, knowingly (seconds of lag, not a live call to Identity); the flag is\ncopied onto products so \"on the shelf\" stays one property (specs/095 research D1-D3).\n\nTests: Identity 188/188 (two red before), Catalog 226/226 with five new suspension tests,\nadmin-users 10/10; four mutations caught; Bruno 281/281 with ban -> 404 -> lift -> 200.\n\nCloses #193\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"88de4db26d4c8fc1a3a3a53b6b9e0190039b457e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/git/trees/88de4db26d4c8fc1a3a3a53b6b9e0190039b457e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/git/commits/5ca38919469a1c07b40bec4960a8fa147367d82a","verification":{"payload":"tree 88de4db26d4c8fc1a3a3a53b6b9e0190039b457e\nparent ad095c048e3b323adfdf66115665c6189846b007\nauthor Dũng Hoàng <139071865+jessiicamaru@users.noreply.github.com> 1790468834 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790468834 +0700\n\nfix(catalog): a banned seller''s shop is closed (#202)\n\nA banned seller''s products stayed on sale; their orders became sales nobody could ship (#193).\n\nIdentity publishes SellerSuspensionChangedEvent in the ban''s transaction for a seller, and\nagain when the ban is lifted; a lock closes nothing. Catalog records it on its sellers read\nmodel with an upsert guarded on the decision''s time and copies it onto the seller''s products\n(products.SellerSuspended), so Product.OnShelf answers no for the listing, lookup, images,\nreviews, questions, saving and both pricing paths. Reopening tells savers of products back on\nsale. Approving a banned applicant''s shop is 409; the users page reads \"Banned · shop closed\".\nMigration SellerSuspension is expand-only.\n\nDecided on the user''s behalf: a ban closes the shop and a lock does not; the suspension is a\nread model that decides, knowingly (seconds of lag, not a live call to Identity); the flag is\ncopied onto products so \"on the shelf\" stays one property (specs/095 research D1-D3).\n\nTests: Identity 188/188 (two red before), Catalog 226/226 with five new suspension tests,\nadmin-users 10/10; four mutations caught; Bruno 281/281 with ban -> 404 -> lift -> 200.\n\nCloses #193\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquGLiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAY2EQACR5gin9Qn/UFb1sgBfCGq1T\n37pr5cAgOw0Ch7KcMIvPDiAti1Qt57KNU4UMeY7+7TlKROFrsN96EKQRFcC9ww98\ngkFK0Gxcl8jvdOsdiG6wbQ+pVUFtXgiM/lC7p5EyURAvoV+GDZMTyBGZtRnec/8N\nPUl4OurVJrbEpy629V1Wp9VfFlqpBod5p5aa7UwdRkYlG4fc5zGqBgIria6YrzEo\nB3tgj7moud0zmHC2XoXo2IjrGG2s7ng/De5TSVQTkGpc8PMYajMwjLjsYB2Bj/k8\nUUERaOZfGRoPhE8g3niQ+L7KjhAV7OUfBt+y/Zb2dECDc1XhIaerIRYEl04jiyPM\nXP8EE/qeY8kFOTT4yXQSSjR6i8awaIjubD8ho1M8YBhuSyrfPWPBaP0I9dTLXiUo\nWPH/5QLpqTAVoDDJ4m4HemC99zgRU4n+OcyFdLVuUhoG/cN25/g3Zz+yTMbyc+KY\nsphTrIAOvCk2LiIh/8ADulE7sLy82qKy9ht70OIOciQ7bmslZQIJxYgWSSLcZELd\ndmU3Ty3xZtNHpM/zuFaYAAGdrE0yQEeqDw53ur3flMcxL4Xy3bF97OudjpxI51OG\n6sbnHEPi+LoVw9jliLpWu3XEQI/J6X0FGgaU82Cll8tDPryyk8HXFbjsH2P3p/Qr\nw7CIjTATcDE8WR1QKiTY\n=y7cW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T00:27:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commit/5ca38919469a1c07b40bec4960a8fa147367d82a","node_id":"C_kwDOUJVo4NoAKDVjYTM4OTE5NDY5YTFjMDdiNDBiZWM0OTYwYThmYTE0NzM2N2Q4MmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commit/ad095c048e3b323adfdf66115665c6189846b007","sha":"ad095c048e3b323adfdf66115665c6189846b007","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/ad095c048e3b323adfdf66115665c6189846b007"}],"sha":"5ca38919469a1c07b40bec4960a8fa147367d82a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/5ca38919469a1c07b40bec4960a8fa147367d82a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139071865?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jessiicamaru","id":139071865,"login":"jessiicamaru","node_id":"U_kgDOCEoReQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jessiicamaru","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/commits/ad095c048e3b323adfdf66115665c6189846b007/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T00:12:06Z","email":"139071865+jessiicamaru@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dũng Hoàng"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T00:12:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: hold seven promised behaviours with tests, and page the staff review list (#201)\n\nFourteen tests for the seven behaviours of #186 that were fixed or promised but held by no\ntest - reset and restore toasts after a remount, the wording fallback when Activity is down,\na tax rate changed after an order, the saga''s currency and variant relay, simultaneous email\nretries, the approved shop''s name and simultaneous shop applications - each shown red by a\nmutation that reverts it. The staff review list gains the 1-50 paging rule every other\nCatalog list has (GetReviewsForStaffQueryValidator); a page of 100,000 was one response.\n\nRow 2''s fallback turned out to have two independent guards (the data-only effect and the\nbundle-first merge); only breaking both blanks a notice (specs/094 research D3).\n\nAlso: a Bruno request for the staff list''s 400, CLAUDE.md''s test counts, and #193-#200 from\nthe management and delivery audit added to the backlog.\n\nTests: Identity 184, Order 268, Orchestrator 18, Catalog 221; storefront 472, lint and types\nclean; Bruno 276/276; verify-saga pass.\n\nCloses #186\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"be2b18b7fd4f194b3c9c83c443937c42f4a7ef84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/git/trees/be2b18b7fd4f194b3c9c83c443937c42f4a7ef84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jessiicamaru/e-commerce-asp-dotnet-practice/git/commits/ad095c048e3b323adfdf66115665c6189846b007","verification":{"payload":"tree be2b18b7fd4f194b3c9c83c443937c42f4a7ef84\nparent 0026aa737e2288061c744b535a49744a3a6f446e\nauthor Dũng Hoàng <139071865+jessiicamaru@users.noreply.github.com> 1790467926 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790467926 +0700\n\ntest: hold seven promised behaviours with tests, and page the staff review list (#201)\n\nFourteen tests for the seven behaviours of #186 that were fixed or promised but held by no\ntest - reset and restore toasts after a remount, the wording fallback when Activity is down,\na tax rate changed after an order, the saga''s currency and variant relay, simultaneous email\nretries, the approved shop''s name and simultaneous shop applications - each shown red by a\nmutation that reverts it. The staff review list gains the 1-50 paging rule every other\nCatalog list has (GetReviewsForStaffQueryValidator); a page of 100,000 was one response.\n\nRow 2''s fallback turned out to have two independent guards (the data-only effect and the\nbundle-first merge); only breaking both blanks a notice (specs/094 research D3).\n\nAlso: a Bruno request for the staff list''s 400, CLAUDE.md''s test counts, and #193-#200 from\nthe management and delivery audit added to the backlog.\n\nTests: Identity 184, Order 268, Orchestrator 18, Catalog 221; storefront 472, lint and types\nclean; Bruno 276/276; verify-saga pass.\n\nCloses #186\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquF9WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAH60QAGxR81PBsZxbIDkONpb8qJhd\nyCh6d0Wy+8cYdfZeebKQ9B1U5q9cfN5wXvaFdR8tomBU